[{:db/id "q-334867/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "a9eb204e-c70d-54d4-b742-f513048a08b6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334867/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "a98ac62f-f058-57ac-8335-a15f9724ddb6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334867/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "0cee747c-bc60-5e87-a679-0c290c9c6034" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334867/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "0974819d-0b6d-5aad-9dba-2ce912959e1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334867/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "012dab08-5bc7-5382-be68-12dcc9a3542b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334867/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc7501d8-9c50-5faa-86db-a943f1bb2057" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334867/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-334867/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-334867/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-334867/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-334867/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-334867/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334867" :question/id #uuid "0432fb7b-7daa-53b5-90f8-a5e72262915a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334867" :question/problem "Suppose $f(x)=-2{x}^{2}+{e}^{x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0$\n- $f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0$\n- $f=O({x}^{2})$ as $x\\to 0$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we wish to test whether the following statement is true:\n\n$$\nf(x)=O(g(x))\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nTo do this, we can examine the limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to a}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)}.\n$$\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- If the limit is *finite*, the statement is true.\n\n- If the limit is *infinite*, the statement is false.\n\n- If the limit does not exist, the test is inconclusive.\n\nHere, we must consider the function\n\n$$\nf(x)=-2{x}^{2}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Let $g(x)=1.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to a}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(-2{x}^{2}+{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Let $g(x)=x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to a}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(-2x+\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNear $x=0,$ we have ${e}^{x}≈1,$ so\n\n$$\n\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x}≈\\frac{1}{x},\n$$\n\nwhich becomes arbitrarily large in magnitude as $x\\to 0.$\nThus,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}(-2x+\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x})=\\infty .\n$$\n\nHence, $f\\ne O(x)$ as $x\\to 0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Let $g(x)={x}^{2}.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to a}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(-2+\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{2}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{x}≈1$ near $x=0,$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{2}}≈\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhich becomes arbitrarily large in magnitude as $x\\to 0.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}(-2+\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{2}})=\\infty .\n$$\n\nThus, $f\\ne O({x}^{2})$ as $x\\to 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334867/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b841cdab-5473-5eeb-a02a-1d1acbae2984"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334867"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335020/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "e37ade1e-058a-53f8-ba30-aa266c62084a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335020/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "418c4797-b1f1-5f86-98be-0f6440a5593f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335020/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "7cd1d1ce-eda9-5542-9461-b2f4d925c669" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335020/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "7d868102-8db9-5be3-bdc0-5855ebfcbf2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335020/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "4ac76b12-90e2-5a34-b485-ca858e01aa31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335020/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2f3c6f6-849b-58b1-997c-8d2d84e818ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335020/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-335020/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-335020/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-335020/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-335020/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-335020/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335020" :question/id #uuid "bb2dcc43-be7e-5d30-a224-0c93857a866f" :question/math-academy-id "q-335020" :question/problem "Suppose $f(x)=2{x}^{4}+5{x}^{2}+10.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f=O({x}^{5})$ as $x\\to \\infty $\n- $f=O({x}^{2})$ as $x\\to \\infty $\n- $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty $" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we wish to test whether the following statement is true:\n\n$$\nf(x)=O(g(x))\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nTo do this, we can examine the limit\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to a}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)}.\n$$\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- If the limit is *finite*, the statement is true.\n\n- If the limit is *infinite*, the statement is false.\n\n- If the limit does not exist, the test is inconclusive.\n\nHere, we must consider the polynomial\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{x}^{4}+5{x}^{2}+10.\n$$\n\nNow, let us analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Let $g(x)={x}^{5}.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2{x}^{4}+5{x}^{2}+10}{{x}^{5}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{10}{{x}^{5}}) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f=O({x}^{5})$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\n- Statement II is false. Let $g(x)={x}^{2}.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2{x}^{4}+5{x}^{2}+10}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(2{x}^{2}+5+\\frac{10}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f\\ne O({x}^{2})$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\n- Statement III is true. Let $g(x)=1.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2{x}^{4}+5{x}^{2}+10}{1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(2{x}^{4}+5{x}^{2}+10) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f\\ne O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335020/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b841cdab-5473-5eeb-a02a-1d1acbae2984"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335020"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335048/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "696b2e76-27c8-5820-a7c4-7e01deae5cf8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335048/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "9a83a6aa-951d-5e9b-a030-349dd4ebfbf1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335048/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "d1eebab7-2f00-55e8-bcd5-3019876eab52" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335048/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "8bb3ddaf-3f36-59dc-8dcc-9e9ef1352442" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335048/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "d9464860-7fd9-5e3c-9c31-dfdc3e138629" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335048/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eac693ab-03c7-5c64-ac12-0b75caae58b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335048/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-335048/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-335048/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-335048/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-335048/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-335048/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335048" :question/id #uuid "265a0e7d-50b1-599b-b8a6-59c58750a06d" :question/math-academy-id "q-335048" :question/problem "Suppose $f(x)={e}^{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty $\n- $f=O(x)$ as $x\\to \\infty $\n- $f=O({e}^{x})$ as $x\\to \\infty $" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we wish to test whether the following statement is true:\n\n$$\nf(x)=O(g(x))\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is either finite or $+\\infty .$ To do this, we can examine the following limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to a}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)}.\n$$\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- If the limit is *finite*, the statement is true.\n\n- If the limit is *infinite*, the statement is false.\n\n- If the limit does not exist, the test is inconclusive.\n\nHere, we must consider the function\n\n$$\nf(x)={e}^{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Let $g(x)=1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({e}^{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f\\ne O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\n- Statement II is false. Let $g(x)=x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince direct evaluation leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ we can evaluate the limit using L'Hopital's rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{({e}^{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{′}}{(x)^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{({e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{x})}{1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\infty +0 \\\\  & =\\infty \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f\\ne O(x)$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\n- Statement III is true. Let $g(x)={e}^{x}.$ Then, using L'Hopital's rule where needed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}) \\\\  & =1+{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =1+{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{′}}{({e}^{x})^{′}} \\\\  & =1+{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1/x}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =1+{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{x{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =1+0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f=O({e}^{x})$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335048/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b841cdab-5473-5eeb-a02a-1d1acbae2984"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335048"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186157693 :question/answer-fields 17592186155356] {:db/id "q-335368/field-1/ma-v1/11821bb6d0a1d90db245ac43bdd4d20971be823de5e896a740ccd3684a4d5629/f7904e4abd2e760d315dab4cf897a31d3c46f02214570396d50f7186584a115b" :answer/id #uuid "cfda5af2-f4db-58a6-93de-60dcb83160fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L1 and L2 only}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335368/field-1/ma-v1/11821bb6d0a1d90db245ac43bdd4d20971be823de5e896a740ccd3684a4d5629/03195e35afe4b349e2790d73af0e27179543506ff31b65c8b6c046209ff0ab7a" :answer/id #uuid "50284454-a60e-5e53-85e9-08805c980070" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L1, L2, and L3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335368/field-1/ma-v1