answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335368/field-3/ma-v1/183a62dbcd1ea51b34da0e0a5ec3c128948f52edddb9153529c00e4afa640736/124b0c2eb11420d91f7684989e46375a3c1c904a04910b2d823439550b297bf2" :answer-field/choices ["q-335368/field-3/ma-v1/183a62dbcd1ea51b34da0e0a5ec3c128948f52edddb9153529c00e4afa640736/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae" "q-335368/field-3/ma-v1/183a62dbcd1ea51b34da0e0a5ec3c128948f52edddb9153529c00e4afa640736/042168976629a933b0d0ef460bdad0013cb33b8a34cdbca393ce80067da1046d" "q-335368/field-3/ma-v1/183a62dbcd1ea51b34da0e0a5ec3c128948f52edddb9153529c00e4afa640736/124b0c2eb11420d91f7684989e46375a3c1c904a04910b2d823439550b297bf2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186155346 :answer-field/correct 17592186155347 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-335368"] :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=4{x}^{2}-x+5,$ then $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0.$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,4{x}^{2}=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,-x=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,5=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(3)$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-1}}  \nand  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line  \n{{field-3}}  \nand  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property. \n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\nWe first observe that each term\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2},\\,-x,\\,5\n$$\n\nis bounded near $x=0.$ Thus, each of the lines\n\n$$\n\\text{L1}:\\,4{x}^{2}=O(1),\\,\\text{L2}:\\,-x=O(1),\\,\\text{L3}:\\,5=O(1)\n$$\n\nis valid as $x\\to 0.$\n\nNext, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From lines $\\text{L1},\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$ we know that each term in\n\n$$\nf(x)=4{x}^{2}-x+5\n$$\n\nis $O(1).$ Thus, by lines $\\text{L1, L2, and L3}$ and the $\\text{sum property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(1+1+1)=O(3)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(3)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nSince $3$ is just a constant multiple of $1,$ it follows by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ that\n\n$$\nf=O(1)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335368/field-1/ma-v1/11821bb6d0a1d90db245ac43bdd4d20971be823de5e896a740ccd3684a4d5629" "q-335368/field-3/ma-v1/183a62dbcd1ea51b34da0e0a5ec3c128948f52edddb9153529c00e4afa640736"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-1/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" :answer/id #uuid "0dfff8f6-1411-543e-8598-0337e0945799" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-1/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" :answer/id #uuid "238faedc-4edf-591b-a924-03267fb55ed2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the sum property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-1/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" :answer/id #uuid "e9321d1a-7966-5813-8f4f-53824adae536" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-1/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" :answer/id #uuid "e62ed3f5-ac97-5525-aa28-18b8e605957b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-1/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" :answer/id #uuid "8cebf043-d2a2-51d3-98e8-cb29d45c6a42" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2725d9c-6314-57bf-94b8-a7ca6acecca9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335468/field-1/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" :answer-field/choices ["q-335468/field-1/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" "q-335468/field-1/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" "q-335468/field-1/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" "q-335468/field-1/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" "q-335468/field-1/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-2/f3a9d801ccdd6cc1c09cebcca8041cf8701bcfc1cf625c969828c0ba6bc74018" :answer/id #uuid "6c7b2f33-d0c1-5b67-8341-7f15d01f81e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-2/314a8bf3988f29de8fd66f4fbfe199e21705e2d339ca177314f13a77b18830f3" :answer/id #uuid "44ef7936-803b-5f7c-a603-d81ced775bc1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$