le property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-5/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" :answer/id #uuid "eb9e1b63-9047-5481-878e-2f186b9ed273" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-5/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" :answer/id #uuid "f46c1a4a-1b6d-507b-9c2b-17a4fa763e76" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the sum property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-5/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" :answer/id #uuid "0661e27c-b760-5ecd-b8d9-681479e3e254" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468/field-5" :answer-field/id #uuid "9630b68a-3196-5137-8e3c-1d6f38af2c66" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335468/field-5/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" :answer-field/choices ["q-335468/field-5/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" "q-335468/field-5/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" "q-335468/field-5/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" "q-335468/field-5/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" "q-335468/field-5/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335468" :question/id #uuid "fe0fc043-68d7-5d3e-9605-f458a82574a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-335468" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{-x},$ then $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O\\,({e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{-x})$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=O\\,({e}^{-x})$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,f=O({e}^{-x})$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,{e}^{-x}=O(1)$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(1)$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines \n{{field-4}} and \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property. \n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O\\,({e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{-x})\n$$\n\nand this is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L3}.$ From line $\\text{L1},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O\\,({e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{-x})\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=O\\,({e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L2}$ and $\\text{the absorption property},$ we have \n\n$$\nf=O\\,({e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{-x})=O\\,({e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L3},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O({e}^{-x})\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L4},$ we have\n\n$$\n{e}^{-x}=O(1).\n$$\n\nThus,  by lines $\\text{L3 and L4}$ and $\\text{the transitive property},$ we have \n\n$$\nf=O(1).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335468/field-1" "q-335468/field-2" "q-335468/field-3" "q-335468/field-4" "q-335468/field-5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe4292f-7653-5486-975e-c206acae734e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335468"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
